WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.286
Architecture includes consequential decisions,
especially those that are difficult to reverse and

00:00:06.286 --> 00:00:07.842
strongly affect quality.

00:00:07.842 --> 00:00:12.702
A box diagram is useful, but ask why the boundaries
and dependencies exist.

00:00:12.702 --> 00:00:19.118
For an alerting service, durable acknowledgments and
a working recovery path may matter more than a

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.868
fashionable component name.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.655
Always connect the decision to its context.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.581
Start with customer outcomes.

00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:31.222
The lecture’s observability pipeline must ingest
data before it can alert on that data.

00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:37.253
Durable storage, service availability and ingestion-
to-alert latency are different qualities.

00:00:37.253 --> 00:00:43.673
Preserving accepted data is valuable even when a
dashboard is unavailable, but it does not make the

00:00:43.673 --> 00:00:44.710
outage harmless.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.693
Set priorities explicitly for the application.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.180
The historical outage illustrates a correlated
failure.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.052
A networking update affected many machines through a
shared change mechanism.

00:00:56.052 --> 00:00:58.519
Replication did not isolate that cause.

00:00:58.519 --> 00:01:04.403
Recovery then differed across environments because
replacing a node and rebooting it preserve

00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:05.416
different state.

00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:11.300
Review the entire control and update path, and
document what each recovery action destroys or

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:11.806
retains.
